findings.description:
Only the sender-mismatch path has a new test. There is no coverage for:
- a token response without `access_token`;
- a `/user` response without `login`, or an HTTP error from `/user`;
- a network failure during token exchange;
- an existing Integration with no `sender`;
- an Integration that exists but is not `ACTIVE` (line 497-498).

The MD5 literal `9cae5e88803f35ed7970fc131e6e65d3` is copied into seven places instead of being derived or held in one constant. `responses.calls[2]` (line 257) depends on the exact order of outbound requests. Both will break on unrelated refactors, such as renaming a view class.
